    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nUndofile only tracks changes in neovim not externally. The improvements to undo that are coming will stop the undo history from getting lost but won't track history of all changes in the middle that happened externally.\n\nIf neovim adds API to update undofile with external changes manually and automatically it can make undo more useful and file history will become very powerful tool.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAPI to tell neovim a file is changed manually.\n\n```\nfor added in $add; do\n  echo $added >> $file\n  nvim --updated $file\ndone\n```\n\nNow every change is there in the undo.\n\nIf detailed control isn't needed or you don't own process that is making changes API to watch files automatically will work.\n\n```\nnvim --watch $file\n\n# different process\nfor added in $add; do\n  echo $added >> $file\ndone\n```",
