        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Are you asking for a formal API which allows editing the undotree() ?\n\nNot to edit the undotree only to tell neovim that the file has changed and I want it to save this version of the file. Like git commit but for undofile.\n\n> The \"watch\" behavior that you showed is already possible, by setting the 'autoread' option (Nvim 0.13 / master). Confirm which Nvim version you are using.\n\nI'm using 0.12.3 but autoread is already enabled.\n\nBut I'm looking for a way to do it headless because a process can change a file without someone having it open. This is how I want to tell neovim to update the undofile. The echo should show every undofile changed after each write.\n\n```sh\nnvim --headless --listen /tmp/nvimlisten\n  \nfor added in addline1 addline2 addline3; do\n\n  echo $added >> $changefile1\n  nvim --headless --server /tmp/nvimlisten --remote-send \":e $changefile2<CR>\"\n  echo changefile1 undofile $(ls -l $undofile1)\n\n  echo $added >> $changefile2\n  nvim --headless --server /tmp/nvimlisten --remote-send \":e $changefile2<CR>\"\n  echo changefile2 undofile $(ls -l $undofile2)\n\ndone\n\nnvim --headless --server /tmp/nvimlisten --remote-send \":qa<CR>\"\n```\n\nI can make it work but not in reliable way or headless. I had to open neovim UI in a new tmux window and switch to it the window after `:e` to make the undofile get written. And sleep commands to wait a few seconds.",
